{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>My sabbaths you shall keep, and My sanctuary you shall revere.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Scripture constantly warns about the Sabbath just as it constantly warns about idolatry, for the reason that it is weighed against all the commandments, and whoever does not keep the Sabbath denies the act of Creation." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'My sabbaths you shall keep and My sanctuary you shall revere' — it mentioned keeping for the Sabbath and reverence for the sanctuary. One might think he should be in awe of the sanctuary itself — therefore Scripture says, 'את שבתותי תשמרו.' Just as with the Sabbath, you do not stand in awe of the Sabbath itself but rather of Him who commanded concerning the Sabbath, so with the sanctuary, you do not stand in awe of the sanctuary itself but rather of Him who commanded concerning the sanctuary. This teaches me only when the Temple stands; from where do I learn when the Temple does not stand? Scripture says, 'את שבתותי תשמרו' — and just as the keeping of the Sabbath is forever, so the reverence for the sanctuary is forever. And they further interpreted this verse in Torat Kohanim: one might think the building of the Temple overrides the Sabbath — therefore Scripture says, 'את שבתותי תשמרו ומקדשי תיראו.'" "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'את שבתותי תשמרו' — I have already explained this in the section of Naso, and also at the beginning of this section; but here it added an explanation when it said 'ומקדשי תיראו,' and it explained through this that the one Sabbath is the great Sabbath, which is זכור, and the other is the מקדש, which is Knesset Yisrael, the mate of the Sabbath, and it is שמור; and therefore it is not fitting that the labor of the Temple should override the Sabbath and the sanctuary, and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:13.651082593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}